reproducible from a single `docker compose build cobol-rekt`.

## Why a re-image?

We re-image (rather than just consume a published JAR) because:

1. The patches in `./patches/` need to be applied at build time.
2. We want a single, version-pinned artefact (`rekt-oss-mma:latest`) so
   demos and CI runs are reproducible without depending on a third-party
   registry.

The image name **`rekt-oss-mma`** = *rekt* (the upstream project name) +
*oss* (open-source distribution) + *mma* (Modernization Modernization
Agents repo, where it lives).

## Contributing patches back

If you improve any of the files under `./patches/`, please also open a
corresponding PR against [avishek-sen-gupta/cobol-rekt](https://github.com/avishek-sen-gupta/cobol-rekt)
where appropriate — the goal is for this patch set to shrink to zero
over time.
